{%- comment -%}
  Shared markup for the `link` atom — the single source of truth for
  what this atom renders. Two callers, and they must not drift:
    - blocks/dm-link.liquid  — as a Shopify theme block (shallow)
    - the inline emitter        — as {% render %} inside a parent's
                                  dm_inline setting, when nesting would
                                  otherwise blow Shopify's depth cap of 8

  Params are flat (not a settings object) because Liquid has no object
  literal, so the inline emitter can only pass key: value pairs.
  Slot content arrives PRE-RENDERED as string params (children, …): a
  snippet can never run `content_for`, so the caller captures it.

  No defaults here, deliberately. A {% schema %} `default` is an EDITOR
  seed — it populates the JSON when a merchant adds a block — NOT a
  render-time fallback. Our templates are machine-generated, so a setting
  the emitter omits (`omitValue`) is simply absent and reads blank. Both
  callers take their values from that same emitter map, so re-declaring
  defaults here would invent attributes that never render today.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign p = closest.product | default: product
-%}
{%- capture href -%}{%- render 'dm-resolve-link', link: href -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  # `bind` (dynamic current-product URL) overrides the static smart-link —
  # but ONLY when a product is actually in scope. On a non-product template
  # (home, landing) nothing declares one: `closest.product` resolves off a
  # section's own `product` setting, which only a product-context Section
  # sets, and the `product` global exists on product templates alone. `p` is
  # then nil and `p.url` is blank, so this used to assign an EMPTY href —
  # `<a href="">` re-navigates to the current page, turning the CTA into a
  # silent self-link. The merchant cannot repair it either: the Inspector
  # disables the Link row while a bind is set. Fall through to the static
  # smart-link instead (`dm-resolve-link` already floors that at `#`).
  case bind
    when 'product.url'
      if p.url != blank
        assign href = p.url
      endif
  endcase
-%}
<a
  data-atom-type="link"
  {% if bind != blank %}data-bind="{{ bind }}"{% endif %}
  href="{{ href | escape }}"
  {% if target == '_blank' %}target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"{% endif %}
  {{ custom_styles_attrs }}
  {% if custom_styles_inline != blank %}style="{{ custom_styles_inline }}"{% endif %}
  {% if margin_top != blank and margin_top != '0' %}data-mt="{{ margin_top }}"{% endif %}
  {% if margin_top_sm != blank and margin_top_sm != '0' %}data-mt-sm="{{ margin_top_sm }}"{% endif %}
  {{ shopify_attributes }}
>
  {{ children }}
</a>
